Error [jet.NonCAbiType]: `#Export(c)` `checked` declares the carrier `Int ParseError!`, which is not a C-compatible return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3203_component_declared_failure.jet:7:12
    |
  7 | #Export(c) checked: fn(value: Int) -> Int ParseError! {
    |            ^^^^^^^
 Why: `#Import` / `#Export` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge, and a C export is infallible: it returns no failure carrier.
 Fix: Handle every failure inside `checked` and declare it `Never!`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3203

